# Share git push commands

After any local code change in this repo, always include the exact git commands the user can run to commit and push — even if they did not ask to commit.

Use the current branch name. Include only the files that were changed for the task. Do not run commit or push unless the user asks.

Example:

```bash
git add src/App.jsx
git commit -m "Short message describing why the change was made."
git push origin main
```
